can select a function here, or        from  outside  the menu you can press <ALT> and the key for  the        appropriate function. The options are:        C - Change directory            Use this so you don't have to CHD to a certain directory            each time you escape to the shell.        H - Hangup modem            This will drop the DTR line to cause the modem to hang up.        O - Options menu            This goes to the options menu - see below.        Q - Quit            This will exit VT-100 and return to the shell.        R - Reset Terminal            This will reset all terminal functions to their default            values.        S - Shell            This will fork a shell. It is here that you will probably do            all of your downloading with KERMIT.        0123456789-,.<ENTER> - Keypad keys on the VT-52 and VT-100             terminals.        SHIFT-1234 - PF1,PF2,PF3,PF4            PF keys on VT-52 and VT-100 terminals.        <UP><DOWN><LEFT><RIGHT> - Arrow keys            Again for VT-52 and VT-100 terminals.        When  using VT-52 and VT-100 emulations, you should not exit the        menu with <ENTER> or a keypad <ENTER> will be sent.===============================================================================                                  Options Menu                                  ------------             On  the options menu, there are 6 options. Press the  first        letter  of  each key to scroll through the values.  The  options        are:        Emulation      : OS9, CRT, VT-52, VT-100        Auto line feed : OFF, ON        Baud           : 300, 600, 1200, 2400, 4800, 9600, 19200        Parity         : None, Even, Odd, Mark, Space        Word Length    : 7, 8        Stop bits      : 1, 2===============================================================================                            Other Useful Information                            ------------------------             When  using systems that use the DELETE character ($7F) you        must use CTRL-;. The left arrow key will send a backspace ($08).             Those  using  the IBM keyboard adapter may notice that  the        SHIFT-2  key  is different (send @ instead of "). This has  beem        taken  into account so ALT-SHIFT-1234 for the PF keys will still        work. Also, ALT-+ is the same as ALT-,.             If you need to use some of the strange keys like CTRL-] you        must  type the key as ALT-CTRL-9. With the IBM keyboard  adapter        it is simply ALT-].             If  you  would like ANY improvements made to this  program,        PLEASE SEND ME MAIL. My addresses are above.             If   you  really  like  this  program  you  may  send  your        contribution  to the US Mail address above, BUT YOU DO NOT  HAVE        TO! (I don't belive in the demands that some authors make).===============================================================================             Included  with the archive is a shell procedure file to set        up  the screen just like V-TERM. It simply changes the  palettes        before  calling  VT100. If you would like to make your own,  the        palette numbers are:             2,10 - text background              0,8  - text foreground             5,13 - text foreground used for boldface             1,9  - menu background             7,15 - menu foreground        You  must change both palette numbers, or the inverse text  will        not work.===============================================================================Converted to OS-9/68000 and KWindows by Brian C. White:    - Detect KWindows and center the window on the screen    - Handles all OS-k baud rates    - Send <DEL> for <BACKSPACE> and <BS> for ALT-<BACKSPACE>    - Fork shell via proper system calls    - Use signals to determine when data is ready (instead of busy-wait)    - Split into several routines for better use of signals    - Compiled with GCC 1.43 and full optimization    - Other things I can't think of ;-)===============================================================================Change History:93/06/09 - Fixed bug with VT100 screen size request (BCW)93/06/09 - Greatly increased scrolling speed (BCW)